POEM1 = ("Harmattan (unseen poem)",
         "The harmattan creeps in on dusty feet,\n"
         "it wraps the town in a grey and silent shawl;\n"
         "the mango leaves hang tired in the heat,\n"
         "and cracked lips wait for rain that will not fall.\n\n"
         "Yet in the compound Grandma hums her song,\n"
         "her voice a thread that stitches dawn to dusk;\n"
         "she says the dry wind cannot stay for long,\n"
         "that every seed lies waiting in its husk.\n\n"
         "So I will keep my hope the way she keeps\n"
         "her rosary of years, bead after bead,\n"
         "until the first fat drop of April leaps\n"
         "and wakes the patient sleeper in the seed.")
